speechtext:
In so far as the Department of Industry, Trade and Commerce is concerned: yes, under the Federal Assistance to the Construction of Convention Centre Program.
1. (a) The total cost of the project is estimated at $16 million.
(b)	The federal government will contribute $3.8 million, the provincial government $3.8 million and the remainder will be provided by the Dale Corporation.
(c)	Terms and Conditions:
(1)	Federal assistance to be limited to the capital costs, including land, of trade and convention centres, and in no case will the federal assistance be used to cover the operating costs of the centres;
(2)	the federal contribution under this program for any one centre not to exceed 25 per cent of the total estimated capital cost, including land, or the contribution of the provincial government concerned, whichever is less;
(3)	in any one year, total federal assistance under this program limited to a maximum of $15 million, including land;
(4)	this federal government initiative not to cover any cost overruns; and
(5)	federal support limited to those centres which have been shown to be economically viable. Selection of qualifying trade and convention centres will reflect the priorities of regional requirements and opportunities.
